\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{An exact rational coupled sum on the sign torus}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{Take #{X=(\mathbb Z/2\mathbb Z)^2},
#{G=C_2}, #{F=\mathbb Q} in the sign representation,
#{m=5} and #{w(U)=1}. Use the counting cochain pairing and
the primary kernel #{K_U=5\bbI+\extD_U}. The
[unnormalized partition coefficient](fdip-00TU), over all
#{2^8=256} link assignments, is
##{Z=9165592232192.}
For the horizontal two-edge loop based at #{(0,0)}, let
#{L_x(U)=U_1(1,0)U_1(0,0)}. Its normalized mean is
##{\langle L_x\rangle=-\frac{330765108}{35803094657}.}
All connection weights are positive by \ref{fdip-00U7}.}

\p{Order the sites as #{(0,0),(1,0),(0,1),(1,1)}.
A spanning-tree gauge sets
#{U_1(0,0)=U_2(0,0)=U_2(1,0)=1}. The remaining signs are
##{\begin{aligned}
 a&=U_1(1,0),& b&=U_1(0,1),& c&=U_2(0,1),\\
 d&=U_1(1,1),& e&=U_2(1,1).
\end{aligned}}
Fixing the gauge at #{(0,0)} determines it uniquely along
the tree. Every full stabilizer consists of the two constant
gauges: each nonzero sign link forces its endpoint gauges
equal. Thus each of the #{32} representatives has an orbit
of size #{16/2=8}.}

\p{The coefficient pullbacks in this gauge are
##{T_1=\begin{pmatrix}
0&1&0&0\\a&0&0&0\\0&0&0&b\\0&0&d&0
\end{pmatrix},\qquad
T_2=\begin{pmatrix}
0&0&1&0\\0&0&0&1\\c&0&0&0\\0&e&0&0
\end{pmatrix}.}
Put #{A=T_1-\bbI}, #{B=T_2-\bbI}.
Order even cochains by degrees #{0,2} and odd cochains by
directions #{1,2}. The even-to-odd block is
##{C=\begin{pmatrix}A&-B^{\mathsf T}\\B&A^{\mathsf T}\end{pmatrix}.}
Block elimination over #{\mathbb Q} gives
##{\det(5\bbI+\extD_U)=\det(25\bbI_8-C^{\mathsf T}C).}
Multiplying the displayed blocks yields exactly the matrix
#{M} of \ref{fdip-00U9}; its determinant is #{P(a,b,c,d,e)}.}

\p{The representative weights have the following finite
distribution, obtained by substituting the signs in that
polynomial. The last column sums their values of #{a}:
##{\begin{array}{r|r|r}
\det K_U&\text{count}&\sum a\\\hline
33871089681&1&1\\
35128130625&1&1\\
35140126849&8&4\\
35152125121&2&0\\
35792477721&8&0\\
36463048209&8&-4\\
36469158961&3&-1\\
37822859361&1&-1
\end{array}}}

\p{Equivalently, summing a nonconstant squarefree word over
all #{32} sign choices gives zero: pair the two values of any
letter occurring in it. Only the constant coefficient of #{P}
survives. The orbit size therefore gives
##{Z=8\cdot32\cdot35803094657=9165592232192.}
The loop has #{L_x=a} in the fixed gauge. In the sum of
#{aP}, only the coefficient of #{a} in #{P} survives.
Dividing by #{Z} gives the displayed mean. Gauge invariance
from \ref{fdip-00TW} makes these representative calculations
equal to the full sums.}

\p{The sum includes curved configurations: #{b=-1} with the
other signs one has the two negative plaquettes of
\ref{fdip-00SM}, translated by one vertical step. Uniform
link counting gives zero mean for #{L_x}; the computed
nonzero mean therefore records the change caused by the
matter determinant.}
